eight bits that are one, eight bits that&nbsp;
are one and eight bits that are one so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:13.760
those first free octets are all representing the&nbsp;
network ID. Now the last octet in the orange box&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:20.320
here is going to be the host ID. That's why it's&nbsp;
zero. So every bit in the subnet mask that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:26.880
zero means that's where we have values that can&nbsp;
